    "answer": {
      "short": "$2\\frac{3}{4}$. Group and add fractions with the same denominator.",
      "worked": "Group fractions with the same denominator to avoid finding a common denominator for all six fractions.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{3}{7}+\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{9}{13}+\\frac{4}{7}+\\frac{1}{8}\n&=\\left(\\frac{3}{7}+\\frac{4}{7}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{9}{13}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{7}+\\frac{13}{13}+\\frac{6}{8}\\\\\n&=1+1+\\frac{3}{4}\\\\\n&=2\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
